    <fr:title text="Decidable Proposition">Decidable Proposition</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    A type <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P]]></fr:tex> is <html:strong>decidable</html:strong> if there is either a term of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P]]></fr:tex> or a
    function refuting <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P]]></fr:tex>. The type of decisions for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P]]></fr:tex> is
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \mathsf {isDecidable}(P):\equiv  P+(P\to \mathbf {0}).
    ]]></fr:tex>
    A term in the left summand supplies evidence for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P]]></fr:tex>; a term in the right
    summand supplies evidence for its negation.
</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
